This repository is the reserved product home of Boussole Politique. It carries a
frozen reference implementation, its specifications, and the dry-run material
built on French parliamentary open data. It is a multi-licence repository.

The licence for each file is declared through REUSE.toml:

- EUPL-1.2: first-party software — the Rust workspace under `crates/`, the
  application host under `apps/` apart from its generated brand assets, the
  workspace manifests and the files under `.github/`;
- Apache-2.0: interoperability and test material — the executable scoring
  vectors, the registered methodology parameters, the dry-run link overrides
  under `dry-run/fixtures/`, and the generic verification and dry-run harnesses
  under `scripts/` and `dry-run/scripts/`;
- CC-BY-4.0: editorial documentation, specifications, methodology analyses and
  first-party project records, including the evidence files under `proofs/`
  apart from the rendered brand proof sheet;
- LicenseRef-Trademark: the visual identity under `assets/brand/`, its generated
  derivatives under `apps/web/assets/` and the rendered proof sheet under
  `proofs/brand/`. These carry **no outbound licence at all**: they are governed
  by the organisation's trademark policy, which reserves the right to alter or
  commercially reuse a mark. See `assets/brand/LICENSE.md`;
- etalab-2.0 (Licence Ouverte / Open Licence): the Assemblée nationale source
  archives under `dry-run/data/`, redistributed as acquired. That material keeps
  the terms of its producer, which permit reproduction, redistribution,
  adaptation and commercial reuse subject to attribution;
- etalab-2.0 AND CC-BY-4.0: those dry-run outputs that redistribute upstream
  records. They are derivative works — the records are the producer's, the
  selection and computation ours — and carry both licences accordingly.

Which dry-run outputs fall under that last point is decided by what a file
contains, not by its extension: an output carries the upstream licence when it
names an individual representative or reproduces a per-record table of
legislative dossiers. Prose and `.json` come out of the same scripts, so the
same test is applied to both, file by file, in REUSE.toml. Outputs holding only
figures we derived are licensed CC-BY-4.0 like the rest of our analyses.

Full licence texts are stored in LICENSES/.

## Attribution of the source data

The Licence Ouverte grants its freedoms on one condition: citing the source and
the date of the last update of the information reused. This repository
discharges that condition as follows.

  Assemblée nationale, open data downloaded from
  https://data.assemblee-nationale.fr/, under the Licence Ouverte / Open
  Licence. Updates of 2026-06-12 (legislature 17: scrutins, dossiers
  législatifs, AMO10) and 2024-06-28 (legislature 16: scrutins, dossiers
  législatifs).

The notice covers the archives and every analysis derived from them, including
those licensed CC-BY-4.0 alone: adapting the information does not extinguish the
attribution owed on it. Anyone redistributing this material or its derivatives
carries the same condition forward.

This attribution confers no official character on the reuse and implies no
endorsement by the Assemblée nationale.

The full provenance record required before publication — source paths,
per-archive SHA-256, update dates, database rights and personal-data analysis —
is in `dry-run/DATA-PROVENANCE.md`.

No licence here grants any right over the names, logos or marks "Libre AI" and
"Boussole Politique".

The organization-wide licensing policy — scope, precedence, historical grants,
data and contribution rules — is the canonical one and is not restated here:
https://github.com/libre-ai/libre-ai/blob/main/LICENSING.md

Historical revisions previously published under MIT remain available under those
terms. No previous licence grant is withdrawn.
